+        <t>Interpreting a query response can depend on which declared sources were searched, the applied matching criteria and time boundaries, whether the applicable search was completed, and any material access or search limitations. Such information can be conveyed in the response or established by an applicable profile together with response-specific information. This allows an auditor to distinguish a completed search with no qualifying records from an incomplete search, without treating either result as proof that the underlying event did not occur.</t>
